## Use a Getter for Read‑Only Computed Values

Instead of calling a method in interpolation (which runs on every change detection), use a TypeScript getter:

```typescript
get fullName(): string {
  return `${this.firstName} ${this.lastName}`;
}
```

Then `{{ fullName }}` will be just as efficient as a simple property.
